+When part of an invoice can't be read, everything that could be read is still returned. Fields that are missing or unreadable are `None` (a line with an unreadable quantity or unit price keeps its other values and has `amount` `None`), they are named in `missing` (e.g. `["invoice_number"]`, `["line 2 quantity"]`), and `status` is `incomplete`. An `incomplete` invoice must never go into the ledger as it is; a clerk fills in only the fields in `missing`. `lines_total` is `None` when any line amount is unknown. `missing` is empty for `ok` and `mismatch`.
+
+If the model's answer can't be read at all, or nothing usable comes out of it, the function raises `InvoiceError`.
 
